1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,037
See these two pieces? Watch.

2
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:07,610
Three moves, and that pair's home.

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:15,161
By the end of this video, you'll be able to do that with any pair. No memorising, just three animals.

4
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:21,719
This is the F2L Hunting Story. So grab your cube, and let's get into it.

5
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:30,085
A quick refresher first. F2L means the first two layers, and you've already got your white cross on the bottom.

6
00:00:30,567 --> 00:00:33,172
Now we pair up a corner with its matching edge,

7
00:00:33,667 --> 00:00:35,793
and drop that pair into its slot.

8
00:00:36,267 --> 00:00:39,578
Do that four times, and the first two layers are done.

9
00:00:40,067 --> 00:00:45,372
To make this stick, we'll tell it as a story. The white corner is our hunter.

10
00:00:45,867 --> 00:00:48,338
The edge with the same two colours is its prey.

11
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:52,971
And this empty slot down here is its den. That's home.

12
00:00:53,467 --> 00:01:00,641
When the hunter catches the prey, they join up. That's the kill. Then it carries its prey home.

13
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:08,471
There are just three rules. First, the top layer is free. Turn it as much as you like.

14
00:01:09,067 --> 00:01:14,162
Second, a side face only turns a quarter turn out, and then it comes straight back.

15
00:01:14,733 --> 00:01:26,314
And third, the golden rule. When a side face turns, one of the slots comes up to the top. Make sure it's the empty den, and never a slot you've already solved.

16
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:36,531
So, which hunter have you got? Look at the top colours of the two pieces. If they're different, like a tiger's stripes, it's a tiger.

17
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:39,581
If they're the same colour, it's a crocodile.

18
00:01:40,167 --> 00:01:45,661
And if the white sticker is pointing up at the sky, it's an eagle. That's all three.

19
00:01:46,233 --> 00:01:52,978
If you'd like to follow along, start with a solved cube. Yellow on top, and green facing you.

20
00:01:53,567 --> 00:01:59,272
Then do these set-up moves. They aren't the solution, they just build the case for you.

21
00:01:59,867 --> 00:02:03,652
So pause the video, and see if you can solve it before I do.

22
00:02:04,633 --> 00:02:15,136
Let's start with the easiest one. Look at the top. There's red on the hunter, and green on the prey. They're different, so this is a tiger.

23
00:02:15,633 --> 00:02:21,004
A tiger always hunts from its den. It's sitting right above the empty slot,

24
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:23,898
and its prey is waiting just behind it.

25
00:02:24,367 --> 00:02:28,575
Watch the tiger. It jumps onto its prey, R,

26
00:02:29,067 --> 00:02:31,260
drags it back over the den, U,

27
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:34,662
and takes it home. R prime.

28
00:02:35,133 --> 00:02:40,110
So why does that work? Well, R swings the hunter round to the back,

29
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:45,952
right where the prey is waiting. That's why the prey has to sit behind it.

30
00:02:46,633 --> 00:02:48,893
Here it is again, at full speed.

31
00:02:49,167 --> 00:02:52,306
Three moves. That's all it takes.

32
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,451
Here's the set-up for the mirror version.

33
00:02:56,433 --> 00:03:02,462
This is the same tiger, mirrored. The top colours are different, so it's still a tiger.

34
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:05,943
But this time, its white sticker faces the front,

35
00:03:06,433 --> 00:03:08,603
so the prey is waiting over on the left.

36
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:13,112
It jumps with the front face this time. F prime.

37
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,578
Drags it back, U prime,

38
00:03:16,067 --> 00:03:18,215
and home. F.

39
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:24,643
Do you see the pattern? Every R becomes F prime, and the U turns go the other way.

40
00:03:25,333 --> 00:03:28,895
So once you've learned one side, you get the other one for free.

41
00:03:29,567 --> 00:03:32,489
Set this one up, and have a go before I show you.

42
00:03:34,733 --> 00:03:44,532
Now, this one's a bit different. There's green on top of the hunter, and green on top of the prey. Same colour, so it's a crocodile.

43
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:51,088
And crocodiles don't chase. They hide under the water, and wait for the prey to come to them.

44
00:03:51,567 --> 00:03:56,676
First, turn the top so the white sticker faces right. U prime.

45
00:03:57,167 --> 00:04:04,525
Now it dives under, R. And notice, it's the empty den that comes up, so nothing gets broken.

46
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,191
The prey walks right over the hidden crocodile. U.

47
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:13,230
And then, it strikes. R prime.

48
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:20,141
Now we take it home. Swing the pair away from the den first. U two.

49
00:04:20,633 --> 00:04:26,375
Then open the den, R, slide it in, U prime, and close it, R prime.

50
00:04:26,867 --> 00:04:32,399
Here's the big idea. While the crocodile's hidden, turning the top can't touch it.

51
00:04:33,067 --> 00:04:38,205
So you can walk the prey exactly where you want it, and then bring the hunter back up beside it.

52
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:43,905
Full speed now. Hide, wait, strike, and home.

53
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:47,724
The set-up moves are on screen, as always.

54
00:04:50,033 --> 00:04:54,366
Red on top, and red on top. Another crocodile.

55
00:04:54,833 --> 00:04:59,415
This time we turn its white sticker to the front, so it dives through the front door.

56
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:02,865
Turn it to face the front. U.

57
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:05,178
It dives, F prime,

58
00:05:05,667 --> 00:05:07,897
the prey walks over, U prime,

59
00:05:08,367 --> 00:05:10,923
and it strikes. F.

60
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:13,315
Swing it away, U two,

61
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:18,020
and take it home. F prime, U, F.

62
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:25,088
It's the same story, just mirrored. If you've got the first crocodile, you've already got this one.

63
00:05:25,767 --> 00:05:28,069
And here's the set-up for our last hunter.

64
00:05:30,733 --> 00:05:37,274
Last one. The white sticker is pointing straight up at the sky. That's an eagle.

65
00:05:37,767 --> 00:05:42,466
Eagles hunt from the air, so first, the prey has to come down to the ground.

66
00:05:42,933 --> 00:05:49,699
Look at the prey's side colour. It's red, so line it up over the red centre. U.

67
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:56,851
Its top colour is green, so we turn the red side away from green, R. And down it goes.

68
00:05:57,333 --> 00:06:00,697
Now the eagle flies over. U two.

69
00:06:01,167 --> 00:06:03,759
And grabs it. R prime.

70
00:06:04,233 --> 00:06:06,042
Swing the pair away, U,

71
00:06:06,567 --> 00:06:11,223
and take it home. R, U prime, R prime.

72
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:17,629
Why away from green? Because turning the other way would lift a slot you've already solved.

73
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:25,164
And it works wherever the prey starts. Line it up first, then fly until the eagle's right above it.

74
00:06:25,833 --> 00:06:31,477
Full speed. Line up, drop, fly over, grab, and home.

75
00:06:32,467 --> 00:06:43,040
You've met all three hunters now. But so far, the prey was always waiting in just the right spot. In a real solve, it could be anywhere on top.

76
00:06:43,633 --> 00:06:53,577
Each hunter needs its prey in one spot, called the kill zone. For this tiger, that's right behind it. But the prey is over on the left.

77
00:06:54,167 --> 00:06:57,834
And just turning the top won't help, because the tiger turns with it.

78
00:06:58,433 --> 00:07:01,431
So the hunter hides first, just like the crocodile,

79
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,747
the prey walks into place,

80
00:07:04,333 --> 00:07:07,023
and the hunter comes back up, ready to hunt.

81
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:12,076
Here's the set-up for this one. Have a go first, if you like.

82
00:07:13,067 --> 00:07:18,910
It's our tiger from the start. Red on top of the hunter, and green on top of the prey.

83
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:26,055
But the prey isn't behind it. It's over on the left, so this time, the tiger has to chase it.

84
00:07:26,533 --> 00:07:30,649
First, turn its white sticker to the front. U.

85
00:07:31,167 --> 00:07:39,390
Now it hides, through the front door. F prime. The empty den comes up, so nothing breaks.

86
00:07:39,867 --> 00:07:46,169
While it's hidden, line the prey up with its centre, just like the eagle did. U. Red over red.

87
00:07:46,667 --> 00:07:49,677
The tiger comes back up. F.

88
00:07:50,167 --> 00:07:56,754
And walks back above its den. U prime. Now the prey is right behind it.

89
00:07:57,233 --> 00:08:01,712
So it pounces. R, U, R prime.

90
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:07,784
That's the whole trick. While the tiger's hidden, turning the top only moves the prey.

91
00:08:08,467 --> 00:08:13,425
And the mirror tiger hides through the right side instead, just like the first crocodile.

92
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:19,476
Full speed now. Hide, line up, come back, and pounce.

93
00:08:20,467 --> 00:08:22,509
And here's a crocodile to set up.

94
00:08:25,533 --> 00:08:30,166
Green on top, and green on top. So it's a crocodile.

95
00:08:30,633 --> 00:08:37,952
But the prey is further away than before. That's fine. The crocodile just waits a little longer.

96
00:08:38,433 --> 00:08:41,088
Spin the white sticker to the right, U prime,

97
00:08:41,567 --> 00:08:43,847
and dive. R.

98
00:08:44,333 --> 00:08:52,838
Now walk the prey round, until it's right next to where the crocodile went down. U two. That's its kill zone.

99
00:08:53,333 --> 00:08:55,838
Strike. R prime.

100
00:08:56,333 --> 00:08:58,500
Swing the pair away, U two,

101
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:03,657
and take it home. R, U prime, R prime.

102
00:09:04,133 --> 00:09:11,003
So wherever the prey starts, the crocodile does the same thing. The prey just walks a different distance.

103
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:15,052
And the mirror crocodile does the same, through the front door.

104
00:09:15,733 --> 00:09:20,618
Full speed. Dive, walk, strike, and home.

105
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:29,323
So that's the trick. If the prey's in the wrong spot, hide the hunter, walk the prey into place, and bring the hunter back.

106
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:38,637
If it's already touching the hunter, and the colours match on both sides, it's already caught. Just swing it away, and take it home.

107
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:45,054
And if they're touching the wrong way, split them up first. That's coming up next.

108
00:09:45,733 --> 00:09:54,067
Now, sometimes a piece gets stuck in the den, or the two pieces are stuck together. Don't worry, there's an easy way out.

109
00:09:54,567 --> 00:09:55,514
Lift it out,

110
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:56,991
step it clear,

111
00:09:57,467 --> 00:09:58,798
and put the face back.

112
00:09:59,267 --> 00:10:08,243
And here's the trick. Lift it so it comes up as a tiger, with the prey right behind it. Then you already know how to finish.

113
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:10,352
Set this one up first.

114
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:16,205
Here, the hunter's stuck in its den, and it's twisted the wrong way.

115
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:20,315
Lift it out with the front face. F prime.

116
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,319
Step it clear, U,

117
00:10:22,833 --> 00:10:25,607
and put the face back. F.

118
00:10:26,100 --> 00:10:34,711
And look, it's a tiger, with its prey right behind it. You know this one. R, U, R prime.

119
00:10:35,633 --> 00:10:37,387
Here's the set-up for the next one.

120
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:46,071
This time, the prey is stuck in the den, flipped the wrong way. The hunter's waiting at the back.

121
00:10:46,567 --> 00:10:49,568
Lift the prey out. F prime.

122
00:10:50,067 --> 00:10:51,936
Move it clear, U two,

123
00:10:52,433 --> 00:10:55,561
put the face back, F, and there's another tiger.

124
00:10:56,033 --> 00:11:00,512
So it pounces. R, U, R prime.

125
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,765
And the set-up for the last one.

126
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:11,661
In this one, they're touching, but they're joined the wrong way. So first, we split them up.

127
00:11:12,133 --> 00:11:14,854
Hide the prey. F prime.

128
00:11:15,333 --> 00:11:17,192
Walk the hunter away, U,

129
00:11:17,733 --> 00:11:21,617
and bring the prey back. F. Now they're apart.

130
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:25,799
Walk the tiger round to its den. U two.

131
00:11:26,267 --> 00:11:30,544
And pounce. R, U, R prime.

132
00:11:31,033 --> 00:11:40,064
Did you notice? Every time we lifted something, it was the empty den that came up. That's the golden rule, every time.

133
00:11:40,733 --> 00:11:49,542
Let's recap. Different colours on top? That's a tiger. Jump, drag back, and home.

134
00:11:50,133 --> 00:11:57,051
The same colours? Crocodile. Hide, let the prey walk over, then strike.

135
00:11:57,633 --> 00:12:04,357
White sticker up? Eagle. Line up, drop, fly over, and grab.

136
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:11,331
Prey in the wrong spot? Hide the hunter, walk the prey into place, and bring the hunter back.

137
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:21,195
And if anything's stuck, lift it out so it comes up as a tiger. Just remember the golden rule. Only ever lift the empty den.

138
00:12:21,767 --> 00:12:27,413
Don't worry if it feels slow at first. Everyone's F2L is slow at first.

139
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:31,787
Say the story out loud as you turn, and the speed will come on its own.

140
00:12:32,267 --> 00:12:38,421
Which hunter gave you the most trouble? Let me know in the comments. Happy hunting.

